.\" The manual page of ush, for both implementations (TODO 2.14). The user guide, ush/docs/USER.md,
.\" is the long form; test_docs checks that every option and subcommand of `ush help` is here.
.TH USH 1 2026-10-29 "ush 0.2.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ush \- the you shell: ask in plain language at the zsh prompt, get the commands that answer it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ush
.RI [ options ]
.BI // request ...
.br
.B ush
.RI [ options ]
.B //
.br
.B ush
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B ush explain
.RB [ \-v ]
.I command ...
.br
.B ush notes
.RB [ \-v ]
.RB [ \-\-last ]
.RI [ question ]
.IR file ...
.br
.B ush ai configure
.RB [ \-\-file ]
.br
.B ush ai status
.br
.B ush ai clear\-key
.br
.B ush allow
.RB [ add | remove
.IR rule ]
.br
.B ush history
.RB [ \-n
.IR n ]
.br
.B ush replay
.IR id | last
.RB [ \-n ]
.br
.B ush help
.br
.B ush \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ush
sends a request in plain language to an AI model and answers it with shell commands.
By default it runs nothing: it proposes one command at a time.
With the zsh plugin the proposal lands on your command line, where you run it with Enter, edit it,
or ignore it; then
.B //
continues with what you ran, its exit status and output.
The model is Anthropic's, with your own API key, or a local Ollama model, with which nothing leaves
the machine.
.PP
In agent mode
.RB ( \-\-run ,
or the setting
.B mode
=
.BR run )
.B ush
runs commands itself: those its policy verifies as read-only at once, every other one only after
you approve it.
.SS Requests
.TP
.BI "ush //" request
Propose a command, or answer.
With the plugin,
.BI "// " request
works without quotes; without it, quote the request, since zsh would expand
.BR ? ,
.B *
and quotes first.
.TP
.B ush //
Continue: send what you ran, its exit status and output, and get the next proposal.
.BI "// " text
after a proposal continues with a remark or a new question.
.TP
.B ush
A session, with zsh's line editing and history:
.BI "// " text
asks, any other line runs as a command whose output becomes context, and
.B exit
or Ctrl\-D ends it.
.TP
.IB command " | ush //" request
Piped input becomes context for the request, up to 200 KB.
.SS The zsh plugin
.TP
.B Enter
runs the proposal in your shell, as if you had typed it; ush records its exit status and output for
the next
.BR // .
.TP
.B Down
explains the proposal above the command line: what each part does, which files and network it
reads and writes.
A command line is explained once and kept; Down again shows the same explanation.
.TP
.B Up
closes the explanation; otherwise it is your history.
.TP
.B Esc
closes the explanation, or else removes the proposal (in vi mode: Ctrl\-U).
.TP
.B Ctrl\-X n
notes on output or files, printed before the next prompt.
On an empty line, or one with only a
.BI # question ,
on the last recorded output; on a command line, it runs the command, records its output and gets
notes on it; on a line naming files, on those files, the other words being the question.
.SS Agent mode
A command runs without asking only if
.B ush
recognises it as read-only, or it matches one of your allow rules, and it uses no shell syntax that
could hide a change, reads no secret file, was not marked as a change, and the checker, if any,
did not flag it.
Every other command is shown with the reason, and you answer
.B y
(run it),
.B n
(don't, with an optional reason for the model),
.B e
(edit, then run your version) or
.B a
(stop the request).
Scripts the model writes are always shown in full and always need approval.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-run
Agent mode: ush runs the commands itself, read-only ones at once, others after your approval; then
follow-up questions.
.TP
.BR \-N ", " \-\-new
Start a new conversation instead of continuing this shell's.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Agent mode, but show the commands it would run, and run none.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-confirm
Ask before every command, including read-only ones.
.TP
.BR \-1 ", " \-\-once
Answer once, without follow-up questions.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Full explanations (summary, parts, notes, ush's verdict); in agent mode, complete command output
instead of the first 12 lines.
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-model " \fImodel\fR"
Model for this run (default from
.BR "ush ai configure" ).
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-effort " \fIlevel\fR"
Anthropic effort:
.BR low ,
.BR medium ,
.BR high ,
.B xhigh
or
.BR max .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-checker " \fImodel\fR"
Checker for this run, or
.BR off .
A checker is a second model that sees only your requests and each proposed command, never command
output; what it flags gets a warning, or needs your approval in agent mode.
A name starting with
.B claude\-
is Anthropic's, any other Ollama's;
.B anthropic:
or
.B ollama:
in front says so explicitly.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BR "ush explain " [ \-v ] " \fIcommand\fR ..."
Explain a command line with the model, without running it; the same as Down on a proposal.
.TP
.BR "ush notes " [ \-v "] [" \-\-last "] [\fIquestion\fR] \fIfile\fR ..."
Notes on files, piped input or, with
.BR \-\-last ,
the plugin's last recorded output: what it is, what stands out, what to do next.
Words that name existing files are files; the rest is the question.
At most 200 KB in all; files in secret locations, directories, special files, binary files and
files past the limit are refused with the reason.
Never as root.
.TP
.BR "ush ai configure " [ \-\-file ]
Set the mode (propose or run), the provider (Anthropic or a local Ollama), the API key or Ollama
URL, the model, the effort and the checker.
The key goes to the macOS keychain, or with
.B \-\-file
(and on Linux) to a file of mode 0600.
.TP
.B ush ai status
Show the provider, model, key source (never the key) and paths.
.TP
.B ush ai clear\-key
Remove the stored API key.
.TP
.BR "ush allow " [ add | remove " \fIrule\fR]"
List, add or remove commands that may run without approval in agent mode, e.g.
.BR "ush allow add kubectl get" .
A rule matches commands whose words start with it.
Rules are refused for commands ush checks itself, for commands that run other commands, and for
commands that change or send data; they are not used as root.
.TP
.BR "ush history " [ \-n " \fIn\fR]"
List recent requests and the commands they ran (default 10).
.TP
.BR "ush replay " \fIid\fR | last " [" \-n ]
Run those commands again, without AI, through the same approval checks;
.B \-n
shows them without running them.
.TP
.BR "ush help" ", " "ush \-\-version"
Show the usage; show the version and the implementation,
.B go
or
.BR python .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
All but
.B NO_COLOR
are ignored when ush runs as root, so
.B sudo \-E
can't redirect a root session.
.TP
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY ", " USH_API_KEY
The API key, before the keychain and the key file.
.TP
.BR USH_PROVIDER ", " USH_MODEL ", " USH_OLLAMA_URL ", " USH_CHECKER
Override the settings for one run.
.TP
.B USH_BASE_URL
Another Anthropic endpoint, e.g. a company gateway.
.TP
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ", " XDG_STATE_HOME
Where settings, history and conversations live.
.TP
.B USH_HANDOFF
Set by the zsh plugin: a directory of mode 0700 with the proposal, what ran and its output.
.TP
.B USH_BARE_SLASH
Set to 0 before sourcing the plugin: no bare
.B // ...
form.
.TP
.B USH_NOTES_KEY
Set before sourcing the plugin: the key for notes (default
.BR ^Xn ;
empty for none).
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
No colours.
.PP
ush never reads
.B .env
files, and removes
.B ANTHROPIC_*
and
.B USH_API_KEY
from the environment of the commands it runs.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/ush/config.json
Settings, mode 0600.
.TP
.I ~/.config/ush/credentials
The API key when it isn't in the keychain; a regular file of mode 0600, or ush refuses it.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ush/history.jsonl
History: requests, commands, decisions, exit statuses, shortened answers; no command output.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ush/sessions/
Propose mode's conversations, one per shell, kept for an hour.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/ush/explanations.json
The newest 500 explanations, keyed by a hash of the command line.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ush/ush.plugin.zsh
The zsh plugin (with
.BR "\-\-prefix " \fIdir\fR:
.IR dir/lib/ush/ );
.B source
it in
.IR ~/.zshrc .
.SH PRIVACY
With Anthropic, each request sends your text, the OS name, your user name, the working directory,
piped input and the output of the commands that ran (up to 32 KB each; in propose mode, of the
proposals you ran).
.B ush explain
sends the command line and your last request;
.B ush notes
sends the files or output it names, up to 200 KB.
Known secret formats, private keys, URL credentials and your API key are redacted first; that is
pattern matching, so read each command on sensitive machines, or use a local model.
With a local Ollama model all of it stays on the machine; with an Ollama cloud model, Ollama
forwards it to ollama.com, and ush says so.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Answered, or a dry run.
.TP
.B 1
An error, or refused.
.TP
.B 2
A usage or configuration error.
.TP
.B 130
Stopped.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B // why is my disk full?
Propose a command; Enter runs it, then
.B //
continues.
.TP
.B ush \-\-run //which process listens on port 8080
Investigate in agent mode.
.TP
.B journalctl \-n 200 | ush notes 'anything unusual?'
Notes on piped output.
.TP
.B ush \-k llama3.2:3b //clean up old docker images
Propose with a local checker model.
.TP
.B sudo ush \-\-run //why does nginx fail to start
Run approved commands as root; needs a root-owned install.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zsh (1),
.BR sudo (8)
.PP
The user and admin guides: https://github.com/gregoryyy/ushell/tree/main/ush/docs
